{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Getting the Job You Want", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Never Too Old", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Third Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - to talk about real possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Second Conditional - to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Third Conditional - to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. <br/>These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If only <span class=\\\"strong\\\">I had studied</span> harder, I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could have been</span> a doctor. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "If only I had studied harder, I could have been a doctor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I would have climbed the corporate ladder by now if I had only taken a chance that time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I would have been happy if I had stayed with so and so.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If only I had done this, then I would have been that. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Future Continuous Tense vs. The Future Perfect Tense ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future Continuous tense to talk about something that will be happening at a specific time in the future.<br/>You use the Future Perfect tense to talk about an action that will be completed in the future before another action in the future.  ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span> tense, the action will have begun before that moment but it will not have finished yet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will be working</span> at 4:00 p.m. tomorrow. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The person will start work at some point in the future and be working at 4:00 p.m. It is not clear when the person will stop working. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the Future Continuous is: <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will</span> + <span class=\"italic\">be</span> + verb <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will be learning</span> at every moment of every day.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span> tense like the Present Perfect tense in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I will finish the work at 9:30 a.m. You can pick up the work at 9:45 a.m. I <span class=\"strong\">will have finished</span> the work by 9:45 a.m.  <br/>The movie will start at 7:15 p.m. You will arrive at the cinema at 7:20 p.m. When you arrive, the movie <span class=\"strong\">will have started</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure of the Future Perfect tense is: <br/>Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will </span>+ (<span class=\"italic\">not</span>) <span class=\"italic\">have </span>+ past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will have sought out</span> new experiences and new opportunities.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " *Notice the position of <span class=\"italic\">not</span>. It comes between <span class=\"italic\">will</span> and <span class=\"italic\">have</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In five years, I will have learned from my mistakes and not dwelt on them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will have embraced change no matter how scary.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will not be working at a job I do not enjoy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will be learning at every moment of every day.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Tell a story to a partner about a time you had to make a big change in your life.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss what you did and how you felt during the change.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Then write about your plans for the next year about a big change you want to make.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to use Future Perfect Continuous and Future Perfect.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your writing to a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss your goals with them and get their opinion of them as well.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I express my feelings and emotions about change.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write goals and identify objectives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I express my goals clearly to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to reinvent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to remake ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are never too old to reinvent yourself. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "climb the corporate ladder", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the series of steps people go through as they gain more power in a corporation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If only I had studied harder, I could have been a doctor, or I would have climbed the corporate ladder by now", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "so and so", "type": "name"}, {"content": "said when you don't know his or her name or you would rather not say the person's name", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I would have been happy if I had stayed with so and so.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "folks ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm here to tell you folks that living in the past is harmful because it keeps you trapped in a world that no longer exists and does not allow you to move forward. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "radical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be extreme", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It may be painful at first, seem radical, perhaps even frightening, but change provides an important aspect that people need: personal growth. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "aspect", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a particular part of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It may be painful at first, seem radical, perhaps even frightening, but change provides an important aspect that people need: personal growth. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to ensure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to guarantee, make sure", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Change ensures that life stays interesting.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le09ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about emotions, opinions and behavior in a work situation. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about hypothetical situations in the past.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have  done. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Are you someone who likes change? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What is the biggest change you have ever made?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feed